  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Hardial vs Govt Food Inspector on 12 August, 2015",
    "facts": "On 28.1.1995, Food Inspector inspected the premises of the petitioner about 5.45 pm at Agna Restaurant near Bhadsapur, Gurgaon. He was found in possession of 2 kg of paneer for public sale contained in aluminium tray. A sample of 600 grams of paneer was taken and thereafter analysis of same was conducted. It was found that it contained milk fat 46.5% against the prescribed standard of 50%. On this basis, prosecution was launched under Section 16 (1) (a) (i) read with Section 7 of the Act. Prosecution produced seven witnesses and report from the Public Analyst. Petitioner examined two witnesses in defence. In the statement recorded under Section 313 Cr.P.C, accused stated that Food Inspector demanded certain food items from him which he refused to give. As a result, he was falsely implicated.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that sentence of the petitioner be reduced to that already undergone in terms of judgment delivered in Krishan Kumar Vs. State of Haryana, (P&H) 2008(3) Hardial vs Govt Food Inspector on 12 August, 2015 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/100845233/ 1 RCR(Criminal) 338.",
